rarchy IDs are validated by indexing code, not declared SQL FKs.&lt;br&gt;{xor} Chunk parent: section or document, within the same index attempt.&lt;br&gt;Stable IDs are unique per attempt; retrieval serves accepted active rows." vertex="1" parent="1" style="shape=note;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#1F2937;fontColor=#1F2937;"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="35" y="1587.984" width="630.25" height="82" /></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram><diagram id="15-index-state" name="15 · Indexing attempt and reusable state"><mxGraphModel grid="0" gridSize="10" page="0" pageWidth="1818.0" pageHeight="1413.0" shadow="0" adaptiveColors="none" scopeDescription="Implemented entities and conceptual associations; database enforcement is stated in the constraint note." schemaConstraints="UML entity model: solid lines are associations; multiplicities describe the named roles, not database integrity. Attributes use [0..1] for optional values and [0..*] for lists. {PK}/{UQ} are schema-key constraints. Enforced relations and scalar-ID mappings are listed below; cross-service IDs are not foreign keys. Audio checkpoints UNIQUE(indexAttemptId,segmentNumber). Graph checkpoint/write keys are compound IDs. EmbeddingCacheEntry is intentionally unconnected: cacheKey derives from kind/stable ID/input hash/model and algorithm versions; no declared FK ties it to a semantic row. attempt: indexAttemptId; Cascade delete (declared SQL FK); checkpoint: threadId + namespace + checkpointId (logical) (scalar-ID association; no declared FK); attempt context: thread identity contains reelId:attemptId:indexVersion (scalar-ID association; no declared FK)"><root><mxCell id="0" style="fontFamily=Helvetica;" value="" /><mxCell id="1" parent="0" style="fontFamily=Helvetica;" value="" /><mxCell id="E04-index-state-e1" value="attempt" edge="1" parent="1" source="AudioSegmentCheckpoint" target="IndexingAtt